      "writtenOn": "2021-11-24T17:09:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Adding Skia specific flags to this is much like the use of set_defaults in our gn build, which lead to the whole namespacing thing with the skia_executable, skia_source_set, skia_* in gn. (Which was done to avoid overloading the global names like source_set, which other projects like third_part might want to use but should have different defaults.) Basically, adding these Skia specific flag deps makes this a lot like the skia_source_set in out gn build. In other words, I\"m fine with generated_cc_atom for now, but this has also become quite Skia specific, so renaming this something like skia_cc_atom would not be amiss. In any event, adding implicit deps here makes this far more Skia specific and less generic.\n\nThat being said, essentially what this is doing is taking the bazel flags we get, translating those into a set of defines and settings for all the Skia code, then implicitly making all the Skia code depend on those to get those defines and settings. This generally seems fine, though I\u0027m sure that if I had spent more time mucking about with bazel I\u0027d have stronger opinions.",
      "revId": "682be71d94280f90b008a07247db3f0c496d1c7b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
